.TH XFMD 1 "2026-09-14" "xfmd @XFMD_PRODUCT_VERSION@"
.SH NAME
xfmd \- native FOX Markdown viewer and editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xfmd
.RI [ directory | file.md | file.txt | file.mmd ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read and edit local UTF-8 Markdown and text files using FOX.
Markdown is rendered natively without a browser engine or network resource loading.
.SH WORK PATHS
Without an argument the expanded tree starts at the home directory.
A directory argument sets the tree root; "xfmd ." uses the current working directory.
A file argument opens the document with its parent directory as the work path.
Double-click the root to widen to home, then to /. Right-click a directory and
choose Set work path. Click a historic work path below the tree to reactivate it.
The 32 most recent distinct work paths persist between runs.
.PP
The .md filter restricts the tree to Markdown. Disable it to see Mermaid files.
The filename filter matches a substring; ? and * act as wildcards.
Matching ignores ASCII case. Filtering searches descendants in the background,
showing matching files and ancestor directories. Refresh rescans the tree.
Directory symlinks are not traversed. File symlinks outside the root are omitted.
Markdown and raw .mmd Mermaid files open internally (case-insensitive suffixes).
Mermaid opens in Preview; Editor/Split and Save preserve the original raw source.
Unsupported Mermaid shows source and a diagnostic. PDF shares the diagram renderer.
Other valid UTF-8 text opens in Editor; HTML opens in the configured browser,
and binary files use OS association. Ctrl+click requests OS association.
.SH HEADING LINKS
Local Markdown links support absolute or relative paths followed by #heading,
or a same-document #heading. Headings match their displayed title or a lowercase
slug with spaces changed to hyphens and punctuation removed. Repeated slugs use
-1, -2 suffixes. Percent-encode spaces and literal # characters in filenames.
Same-file jumps preserve unsaved edits. Missing headings report a diagnostic.
Explicit HTML IDs and full Unicode case folding are not supported.
.SH KEYS
Ctrl+O opens a file. Ctrl+S saves. Ctrl+Shift+S saves under another name.
Ctrl+Z and Ctrl+Y undo and redo. Ctrl+F searches.
Ctrl+1 shows preview, Ctrl+2 the editor, Ctrl+3 split view.
F10 toggles the sidebar. Alt+Left and Alt+Right traverse document history.
F11 toggles fullscreen; Escape leaves fullscreen unless a dialog is active.
Ctrl+Shift+E exports the current buffer as PDF.
Ctrl+Q quits after checking unsaved changes.
Enter and Space activate the current tree node. Right activates leaves;
directories and lazy reference branches retain normal expansion/navigation.
The toolbar order is Editor / Split / Preview. Returning to Split restores the
previous pane proportion; selecting Split again recovers a collapsed pane.
.SH PREFERENCES AND PUBLICATION
Edit > Preferences has Appearance, Scrolling, Document and Programs tabs.
Appearance controls Light/Dark, Comfortable/Compact spacing, Flat/Classic buttons
and UI font size. Changes are previewed live; OK saves and Cancel restores the
active appearance. The toolbar Light/Dark toggle saves only the theme choice.
Scrolling has speed, optional acceleration and an isolated scroll test area.
Document controls A4 margins; Programs selects the executable for hyperlinks.
.PP
Optional style overrides are read from $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/xfmd/appearance.ini
(default ~/.config/xfmd/appearance.ini). Appearance > Reload style file previews
changes. Cancel restores the prior live profile, without editing the external file.
The installed share/doc/xfmd/appearance.ini provides an example.
View > Window wrap or A4 page preview selects layout. Fit page width and Actual size
change only the paged display scale. File > Export PDF exports the full current
buffer, including unsaved edits, using the same A4 layout and fonts as preview.
File > Cancel PDF export cancels before publication. Export does not save the source.
New PDF targets are private (0600); replacement preserves POSIX mode only.
.SH LIMITS
Files must be UTF-8 and no larger than 8 MiB. NUL bytes are rejected.
Local Markdown links and document index navigation are supported. HTTP(S) links
launch the configured browser. Remote resources and scripts are not loaded.
Images are represented by alt-text placeholders. The parser is cmark-gfm with
the table extension. Glyph coverage depends on installed fonts.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xfe (1),
.BR xfw (1),
.BR xfi (1)
